    "turn_text": "you know, you just start to realize like, oh, there is an election. very soon, because by the way, a year and a half is very soon. And that election is for the next president. And I don't think that people understand, because I feel like it's still something we need to drive home, that the election is also gonna be for legislative positions in the Senate, in the House of Representatives, as well as locally. And in the preparation for this, I want us to start really thinking about what does a candidate look like that we want to get behind? And I don't want us to wait until next year. I want us to start thinking about that now. Because we need to wrap our minds around the fact that yes, there are these binaries just bipartisan, you know, Democrat and Republican situations. But as we all know, Everybody is an individual. And when we really get into the weeds of things, you start to see that there are Democrats who operate like Republicans, there are Republicans who operate like the devil. There are Democrats who have switched, who got in under a Democratic ticket and then switched over to be whether you need to be independent or to be Republican so that they can actually help that cause, et cetera. So you can't just book your ticket or hang your hat on what they all the same. That's lazy. It's intellectually lazy. And we don't have the luxury of intellectual laziness anymore. All of us needs to be putting our minds to work at whatever capacity that we have capable to really bring civics into our culture in a real way. This replay of this episode with Ayana Presley's side effects of being a different Democrat is really, I hope, gonna help illuminate the reality that when it comes to these different political parties, people are under these banners oftentimes because they're the only banners to be under, but it doesn't mean that they can't change, diversify, and broaden the spectrum of what these banners mean. Yes, Democrats and Republicans at many times in this country have looked the same. At one point, they were reversed, okay? They were Dixie Crats, and they were the ones who were actually all behind the racism, et cetera, et cetera. So we cannot consider this to be a static existence. It's something that is always moving and shifting, but hopefully we're moving and shifting the needle in a direction that is more for the people and not for corporations. Because that is what is happening for so many politicians. They are being run, they are being ruled, and they are being supported by corporations. Imagine if there were more people out here in support of them. How we would then have just as much power as the corporations to shift and move the way that our legislation is serving us. Iana Presley is a member of the Squad. The Squad is a group of members of Congress who considered themselves to be progressive Democrats, meaning that they are very outspoken about not being run by corporate dollars, about not being run by lobbyists, and about really considering themselves not politicians but of public servants. Some other members of the Squad are Jamal Bowman from New York, Ilhan Omar from Minnesota, Corey Bush from Missouri, and of course, AOC also from New York. but it's not limited to just them. But they really popularized the squad, and we have seen the number grow. And we want to continue to see this number of what a progressive Democrat grows, because maybe at some point it can move beyond being called a Democrat into something that is its own existence and that changes the face of how we are looking at politics. Y'all complained so much about, oh, Democrats and Republicans are the same. Well, let's create space for something different. And in a government that has been so rigid, that space is only going to be created by force of effort and by consistency. I talked here with Diana Presley about what they're doing to make that space. What are y'all doing to support the making of that space? Check it out right here, side effects of being a different Democrat on small doses podcast. A first of all, I just... You have a smolder face that you met. There it is right there.",
