    "turn_idx": 57,
    "turn_text": "Well, first, I would say that where I find where I'm fueled by, where I'm fortified, where I'm emboldened is being in movement, is being in movement is being in community. And it's the power of that movement that has us closer than ever before to seeing student debt cancellation. It's the power of that movement that made Black maternal morbidity a part of the national discourse. It's the power of that movement that recently resulted in that victory in Kansas of Roe and",
